    <!--
        Field-facing copy.

        The screen previously read "Company Portal", "Corporate Applications",
        "IT Helpdesk & Info", "Request IT App Install" and "Latest IT Announcements" —
        the language of a corporate BYOD portal. The person holding this tablet is a
        census enumerator, not an office employee with an IT department: they want to
        know whether the device is working and whether they can carry on, in words that
        mean something to them.

        These strings were also hardcoded in the layouts (53 of them), so they could not
        be translated. Uganda's census is conducted in several languages; extracting them
        is the precondition for ever shipping a values-lg or values-sw.
    -->
    <string name="app_title">UBOS Census Device</string>
    <string name="app_subtitle">Managed by Uganda Bureau of Statistics</string>

